  "review": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "S6 adds automatic signed webhook provisioning after a confirmed active repository registration. Written behavior and graph include configured success and visible polling fallback; retry and uncertain-create recovery preserve registration and unrelated hooks. The S6 recovery contract now states a thirty-second whole-setup deadline, including authentication and paginated hook reads/writes, followed by the existing durable retry. Re-evaluated both rebased snapshots against main366cbb35, including unchanged authored scenarios and old/new source/assertion mappings; the target credential-redaction change is retained, not reverted. Corrected S6 expiration wording: the deadline cancels this attempt\u2019s admission/authentication/hook work and records fallback; it cannot cancel or release an unrelated request\u2019s ownership. New admission assertions cover both reversed polling ownership and managed HTTP/accounting ownership.",
    "implementation": "ReconcileWebhooks reads confirmed Settings on its own lifecycle worker; missing gateway, unsafe secret or GitHub failure becomes a per-repository polling record. EnsureRepositoryWebhook live-lists all hook pages, creates or updates the exact callback and subscribes to nine existing event types with TLS verification and HMAC secret. The packaged admin skill explains automatic hook provisioning with the registration proposal and directs setup failures to the saved Configuration status. The child attempt context spans EnsureRepositoryWebhook, including StartOperation/authentication/list/create/PATCH; cancellation is released before persisting the existing sanitized failure with the still-live outer service context. Upstream nativeSnapshot and RedactNativeProposalEvents remain byte-identical to target main. The combined S1\u2013S5 native inspection/proposal contract keeps credential-redacted snapshots, raw freshness digests, owner-only credential edits and bounded legacy event migration, while S6 only adds independently prepared setup status. Reviewed the current shared transport delta against both main366 and the prior c124 source: dispatch and managed-accounting ownership remain serialized, with caller-context admission and no added request deadline or Store change. Indirect unchanged flow contracts and existing acceptance gaps retain their meanings. Request returns BeforeDispatch when its dispatch admission expires; lockUsage likewise cancels an accounting-gate wait. All dispatch/requestMu users share zero-value-safe channel gates with cancellation checks before and after admission; process flock, request budgets, authentication memoization and HTTP scopes are retained. webhooks.go persists fallback using the still-live outer context.",
    "tests": "ConfirmedRepositoryRegistrationAutomaticallyProvisionsWebhook exercises actual proposal confirmation and ordinary Loop without native turns. FailureRetainsPollingAndRetries asserts HTTP denial recording, real PR API status refresh, retry deadline, restart recovery and no premature repeats; provider and browser fixtures cover safe reuse, lost response, status projection and visible fallback. The S6 public-delivery gap stays open. TestWebhookSetupTimeoutReleasesProviderForPolling stalls Token while holding the shared dispatch lock, starts ordinary RefreshPullRequests concurrently, and asserts real REST/GraphQL title/state/head and successful CI/checks refresh after the child deadline; outer and daemon contexts remain live, failure is saved and a repeat makes no premature auth/API call. Registration test normal and deferred shutdown joins now both fail locally within five seconds. Read the actual upstream NativeInspectionRedactsUnmanagedCredentials, NativeInspectionPreservesSelectorsAndRedactsURLCopies, NativeProposalRetainsRedactedSnapshotAndRawFreshness and NativeCredentialEditsAreRejectedWithoutPersistence assertions: preserved public selectors/nonsecret values, no raw credential copies, invisible credential rotation rejects stale confirmation, zero rejected persistence/writes and exactly one confirmed safe write. All upstream mappings remain alongside webhook assertions. Read TestWebhookSetupTimeoutWhilePollingOwnsProvider: before releasing ordinary auth it reads sanitized polling/error/At/fifteen-minute RetryAt, asserts owner still active, no second auth/HTTP/budget charge and no immediate retry; after release it requires real PR title/state/head plus CI/checks and exact durable request count. TestWebhookAdmissionCancelsBehindManagedHTTP requires a live authentication latch for each of two BeforeDispatch waiters, then cancellation while the index HTTP owner remains active, unchanged ledger/call count, then successful request and peakHTTP1. TestExpiredGitHubAdmissionDoesNoWork checks canceled/expired zero-value admission performs no auth/HTTP/budget work and a later live request succeeds. Existing setup-own-auth assertions remain via the same real API fixture."
  },
